# Minimal(ish) repro for a confirmed, still-UNFIXED bug: a symbol
# defined in a multi-TEXT-symbol assembly (.s) file can fail to
# resolve when pulled from a .a archive, even though it's right there
# in the archive's index and linking the same .o/.5 file in directly
# (bypassing the archive) works fine.
#
# Found building principia-softwarica's typesetting/pic for arm: pic
# calls ANSI signal(), which (APE/lib/ap/plan9/signal.c's _notehandler)
# pulls in APE/lib/ap/arm/notetramp.c (for _notetramp) from libap.a.
# notetramp.c's own siglongjmp() calls longjmp(), which should resolve
# from the SAME archive's setjmp.s member (setjmp.s there defines
# THREE TEXT symbols together: setjmp, sigsetjmp, longjmp -- longjmp
# is third). Instead 5l reports "longjmp: undefined" at link time.
#
# Confirmed NOT the cause: plain archive/duplicate-symbol handling in
# linkers/ar/ar.c's objsym() (reads generically via objtraverse(),
# skips only the specific duplicate symbol found, doesn't special-case
# TEXT vs DATA order); no "duplicate text symbol" warning is ever
# printed while building libap.a. Also not the type-signature check in
# 5l/obj.c's ldobj() (that's a real, separate, working mechanism --
# briefly suspected because forcing a WRONG extern prototype on
# purpose surfaces a "incompatible type signatures" diag through it,
# but that was this test's own mistake, not the real bug: the actual
# failure path never prints that diag, just "undefined").
#
# Confirmed IS the trigger: setjmp.s having more than one TEXT symbol.
# Splitting it into one file per symbol (longjmp.s on its own) makes
# archive resolution work correctly -- applied as the actual fix in
# principia-softwarica (APE/lib/ap/arm/{setjmp,longjmp}.s). 386's own
# setjmp.s has the same three-symbols-in-one-file shape and was NOT
# split, and doesn't hit this -- so whatever's wrong is specific to
# arm (5a/5l/libmach's 5obj.c), not a general iar limitation. Not
# investigated further than pinning the trigger down to this file
# shape plus the archive-indirection (see comment above); a good next
# step would be comparing 5obj.c's _read5() against 8obj.c's _read8()
# symbol-table walk instruction by instruction for what differs on a
# multi-TEXT-symbol object specifically.
#
# Not wired into `mk test` (see ../mkfile's own comment on
# hexfloat_literal.c etc. for the convention): still an open bug, and
# this one additionally needs a principia-softwarica checkout (for the
# real APE headers -- signal.h/setjmp.h/errno.h/string.h -- and its
# prebuilt arm libc.a), which the rest of this repo's tests don't
# assume. Run `mk repro` by hand once picking this up again; it should
# print "longjmp: undefined" (or similar) on the still-broken setjmp.s
# from git history, and link cleanly against the current (split) one.

PRINCIPIA=../../../principia-softwarica
APEINC=-I$PRINCIPIA/APE/include -I$PRINCIPIA/APE/include/arm
LIBC=$PRINCIPIA/ROOT/arch/arm/lib

repro:V:
	rm -f *.5 *.a *.out
	objtype=arm pcc -FTVw -c -D_POSIX_SOURCE -D_PLAN9_SOURCE $APEINC notetramp_orig.c
	objtype=arm pcc -FTVw -c -D_POSIX_SOURCE -D_PLAN9_SOURCE $APEINC signal_orig.c
	objtype=arm 5a setjmp_orig.s
	objtype=arm iar vuD fakelibap.a notetramp_orig.5 signal_orig.5 setjmp_orig.5
	mkdir -p fakelib
	cp fakelibap.a fakelib/libap.a
	objtype=arm pcc -FTVw -c -D_POSIX_SOURCE -D_PLAN9_SOURCE $APEINC main.c
	objtype=arm pcc -L$LIBC -Lfakelib -o repro.out main.5
	echo 'repro.out linked -- bug is fixed (or setjmp_orig.s is already the split version)'

clean nuke:V:
	rm -f *.5 *.a *.out
	rm -rf fakelib
